---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Hero from "../components/Hero.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
	title="About — Lead From The Hip"
	description="[DAVID — one sentence, after the body copy is written.]"
>
	<Hero
		eyebrow="About"
		standfirst={`[DAVID — one sentence on who you are and what you do. Keep it factual and short. Example shape: "I'm David Morris. I've spent [N] years in [field], most of it [doing what]."]`}
		standfirstPlaceholder
	>
		I got tired of <span class="accent">accurate reports that changed nothing.</span>
	</Hero>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-6">The short version</h2>
		<div class="placeholder border border-dashed border-flag bg-flag-soft rounded-[3px] p-6 measure">
			<p class="mb-4">[DAVID — three or four paragraphs. The structure that works:]</p>
			<ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 not-italic">
				<li>
					<strong class="not-italic">Paragraph 1 — What you actually do.</strong> Your
					background in plain language. Not a CV summary; the version you'd say out
					loud to someone at a table.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="not-italic">Paragraph 2 — The specific frustration that
					produced this practice.</strong> You have sat through or delivered assessment
					debriefs that were accurate and inert. Name a real moment if you have one — a
					specific debrief, a specific client, a specific report that went in a drawer.
					Concrete beats abstract by a wide margin here.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="not-italic">Paragraph 3 — What you concluded.</strong> That the
					missing piece was never better assessment. It was the translation into
					behavior, plus the discipline to come back and measure. Say it plainly.
				</li>
				<li>
					<strong class="not-italic">Paragraph 4 — Why the Stoics and the cognitive
					framework.</strong> Brief. The interesting fact does the work: Ellis built
					REBT explicitly on Epictetus, and a derailing pattern under stress is
					functionally a rigid belief firing. You didn't fuse two unrelated things; you
					noticed they were already related.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-4">Credentials</h2>
		<p class="placeholder measure mb-4">
			[DAVID — list only what you actually hold. Certifications, degrees, professional
			memberships. If a credential comes with logo-use or wording rules from the issuing
			body, follow them exactly. Do not list a publisher's instruments in a way your
			distributor agreement doesn't permit — see docs/08-licensing-guardrails.md.]
		</p>
		<ul class="list-disc list-inside flex flex-col gap-1">
			<li class="placeholder">[Credential]</li>
			<li class="placeholder">[Credential]</li>
			<li class="placeholder">[Credential]</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-2">How I work</h2>
		<p class="text-muted measure mb-6">Four things worth knowing before you get in touch.</p>
		<ul class="flex flex-col gap-4 text-ink measure">
			<li>
				<strong>Small practice, by choice.</strong>{" "}
				<span class="placeholder">
					[DAVID — confirm capacity, e.g. "I take a handful of engagements at a
					time."]
				</span>{" "}
				It means I'm slow to start and hard to rush, and it means the person you talk
				to is the person who does the work.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>The measure is included.</strong> Every engagement ends with a
				behavioral re-measure. It is not an upsell and I don't offer a version without
				it.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>You own everything.</strong> Assessments, feedback, notes. Nothing goes
				to your employer without an agreement we write down first.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>I'll tell you if I'm not the right fit.</strong>{" "}
				<span class="placeholder">
					[DAVID — keep or cut, but it's true and it's rare enough to be worth
					saying.]
				</span>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="max-w-[1080px] mx-auto px-6 py-12 border-t border-rule">
		<h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl mb-2">Get in touch</h2>
		<p class="text-ink measure mb-6">
			The fastest route is a short call —{" "}
			<span class="placeholder">[DURATION, e.g. twenty minutes]</span>{" "}
			— to work out whether there's anything here for you.
		</p>
		<div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 items-center">
			<a
				href="[BOOKING URL]"
				class="bg-petrol text-paper px-5 py-3 rounded-[3px] font-medium hover:opacity-90 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-petrol"
			>
				Book a call →
			</a>
			<p class="text-muted text-sm">
				Or email me at <span class="placeholder">[EMAIL]</span>
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
